Consider a \emph{series} of models that share similar architectures and other pretraining/finetuning setups, but differ in model sizes (e.g. T5-small/base/large, etc.). It is usually safe to assume that the model with a larger number of parameters perform better than the smaller one under most aspects. %While it would still be challenging for a more general superiority assumption on models from different model classes, 
More formally, we can assume a partial order (a linear order within one concerned model class) induced by the oracle metric $E(p)$ as illustrated in Equation~\ref{eq:partial-order} and Figure~\ref{fig:secant}: 
\begin{equation}
