To support our claim that CDM is an evaluation metric that works generally for open-domain text generation tasks, we hereby conduct experiments under two distinct scenarios: 1) using CDM to evaluate dialogue systems, representing the tasks with a diverse distribution of outputs; 
2) using CDM to evaluate the commonsense of lexically-constrained generation models, representing tasks with medium to low diversity in the output. 
